An estimated 40,000 prisoners worked on the project, some died from exhaustion. Others, in hell, pulverized granite and were killed by lung diseases many years later. Franco had initially conceived of the valley of the fallen as a gravesite, much less a mass grave, but it would become one thanks to Franco's twisted response to pressure from one of Spain's main allies. The Americans relied on Spain as one of their European partners during the Cold War. And when they heard about Franco's plans for the Valley of the Fallen, they started to get nervous. The monument was shaping up to be pretty confrontational and divisive.
据估计有4万名囚犯参与了该项目，一些人死于精疲力竭。另一些人在地狱般的条件下粉碎花岗岩，多年后死于肺病。佛朗哥最初将烈士谷设想为墓地，甚至不是万人坑，但由于他对西班牙主要盟友之一施加的压力做出了扭曲的反应，它最终成为了一个万人坑。美国在冷战期间将西班牙视为欧洲伙伴之一。当他们听说佛朗哥修建烈士谷的计划时，他们开始感到紧张。这座纪念碑看起来极具对抗性和分裂性。

